xhci: plat: mark Northstar's xHCI as having broken streams

Northstar's xHCI advertises a small primary stream array (MaxPSASize 1,
hcc params 0x02501164), so the UAS driver claims USB 3 disks. Allocating
the streams then fails, the configure endpoint command is rejected with
a Parameter Error, and the disk is left without a driver:

  xhci-hcd 18023000.usb: ERROR: unexpected command completion code 0x11.
  uas 3-1:1.0: probe with driver uas failed with error -12

Set XHCI_BROKEN_STREAMS alongside the fake doorbell quirk for BCM4708
family hosts. The host then doesn't offer streams, UAS steps aside, and
usb-storage drives the disk at SuperSpeed: on a Netgear R7000 a USB 3 SSD
reads at about 149 MiB/s, against about 32 MiB/s at high speed.
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
 	xhci->quirks |= priv->quirks;
 
 	if (node && of_machine_is_compatible("brcm,bcm4708"))
-		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_FAKE_DOORBELL;
+		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_FAKE_DOORBELL | XHCI_BROKEN_STREAMS;
 }
 
 /* called during probe() after chip reset completes */
